Mekong Medicinal Plant Atlas — compilation and code
===================================================

Code and the compiled tables are released under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International licence (CC-BY-4.0), except where a source states otherwise (see below).

Occurrence records
------------------
The Darwin Core Archive and the occurrence GeoJSON layers are released under CC-BY-NC-4.0,
because they include records published under that licence. Each record keeps the licence it was
published with (CC0, CC-BY-4.0 or CC-BY-NC-4.0), given in its `license` field, and that licence
prevails for that record. The records come from GBIF; each remains available from its publisher.

Geospatial layers
-----------------
Mekong basin boundary: CC-BY-4.0, Tiwari et al., doi:10.5281/zenodo.7622998, derived from
  Dang et al. (2022), Science of the Total Environment 831:154833.
Mekong River centreline: rendered from the WWF-Laos ArcGIS service at run time (no licence
  stated, not redistributed); the committed fallback is Natural Earth 1:10m (public domain).
Country outlines and the Natural Earth river: public domain (naturalearthdata.com).
Basemap: CARTO raster tiles, © CARTO and © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL).

Photographs
-----------
iNaturalist, each image used under the licence shown on the page (CC0, CC-BY, CC-BY-SA, or a
non-commercial variant). The photographer's attribution and the licence are displayed with every
image. Non-commercial images may be used only for non-commercial purposes.

Source workbook
---------------
The ethnobotanical, pharmacological and conservation content is derived from a research
compilation whose rows cite their primary sources. The workbook itself is not redistributed.

If you reuse this atlas, cite the version and, once minted, the dataset DOI, together with GBIF
and World Flora Online for the underlying data.
